Message-ID: <BoC2KwhkRQc.rxwKsaZoFAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
In-Reply-To: <BoC2KwhkRQc.SmaMZYOhAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
References: <BoC2KwhkRQc.VbDZDY5dAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com> <BoC2KwhkRQc.SmaMZYOhAAAJ@r-inla-discussion-group.groups.google.com>
Archived-At: <https://groups.google.com/g/r-inla-discussion-group/c/BoC2KwhkRQc/m/rxwKsaZoFAAJ>
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset="utf-8"
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a model is near non-identifiable you get numerical instability. Parallel computing combines with that in complex ways. Basically, when the model is sensitive to numerical floating point effects surprising things happen, and the solution is to improve the identifiability of the model.

Finn

