On Wed, 2017-09-13 at 09:15 -0700, Jonathon Vallejo wrote:
> Thanks, I hadn't thought of that. Can the MEC model handle non-
> gaussian covariates (i.e. can one define a link function)?

meb and mec models (discussed here: S. Muff, A. Riebler, H. Rue, P.
Saner, and L. Held. Bayesian analysis of measurement error models using
integrated nested Laplace approximations. Journal of the Royal
Statistical Society, Series C, 64(2):231–252,
2015.)

can only do Gaussian errors. you can think of other constructions, like

y = a + b*x + gaussian.error

but 'x' is observed indirectly as 'yy' through

yy ~ Poission(exp(x))

such models you can do.

Håvard Rue
hr...@r-inla.org
